    ```
8. `cJSON_IsObject`
    `cJSON_IsObject` checks whether a `cJSON*` is a non-NULL JSON object. Use it before treating `item` as an object. It returns `false` for `NULL` or any non-object type, and `true` only when `(item->type & 0xFF) == cJSON_Object`. Its signature is:
    ```c
    
CJSON_PUBLIC(cJSON_bool) cJSON_IsObject(const cJSON * const item);
    ```
