## Target API Functions

1. `cJSON_IsArray`
​ `cJSON_IsArray` checks whether a `cJSON*` is a non-NULL array item. Use it before treating `item` as an array. It returns `false` for `NULL` or any non-array type, and `true` only when `(item->type & 0xFF) == cJSON_Array`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CJSON_PUBLIC(cJSON_bool)
cJSON_IsArray(const cJSON* const item);
​ ```
2. `cJSON_InsertItemInArray`
​ Inserts `newitem` into `array` at index `which`. Use with a valid array and non-NULL item; negative index fails. If `which` is past the end, it appends. It also rejects corrupted list links.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
/* Update array items. */
CJSON_PUBLIC(cJSON_bool)
cJSON_InsertItemInArray(cJSON *array, int which, cJSON *newitem);
​ ```
3. `cJSON_AddArrayToObject`
​ Creates a new empty JSON array and adds it to `object` under `name`. Use it for object members meant to hold arrays. On success returns the new array; on failure returns `NULL` and deletes the created array.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CJSON_PUBLIC(cJSON*)
cJSON_AddArrayToObject(cJSON* const object, const char* const name);
​ ```
4. `cJSON_IsInvalid`
​ `cJSON_IsInvalid` checks whether a `cJSON` item’s base type is `cJSON_Invalid`. Use it to test an item before other operations. It returns `false` for `NULL`, and `true` only when `(item->type & 0xFF) == cJSON_Invalid`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
/* These functions check the type of an item */
CJSON_PUBLIC(cJSON_bool)
cJSON_IsInvalid(const cJSON* const item);
​ ```
5. `cJSON_DeleteItemFromArray`
​ Deletes the array element at index `which` from `array`. It first detaches that item, then frees it with `cJSON_Delete`. Use on a valid cJSON array; if the index is out of range or the array is invalid, nothing is deleted.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CJSON_PUBLIC(void)
cJSON_DeleteItemFromArray(cJSON *array, int which);
​ ```
6. `cJSON_AddBoolToObject`
​ Creates a JSON boolean child and adds it to an object under `name`. Use it with a valid object; it returns the new item on success. If insertion fails, it deletes the created bool and returns `NULL`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CJSON_PUBLIC(cJSON*)
cJSON_AddBoolToObject(cJSON* const object, const char* const name, const cJSON_bool boolean);
​ ```

