CJSON_PUBLIC(cJSON_bool)
cJSON_IsRaw(const cJSON* const item);
​ ```
4. `cJSON_IsString`
​ `cJSON_IsString` is a type-check helper. Use it to test whether a `cJSON*` is a string item. It returns `false` for `NULL`, otherwise `true` only when `(item->type & 0xFF) == cJSON_String`; it doesn’t inspect the string contents.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CJSON_PUBLIC(cJSON_bool)
cJSON_IsString(const cJSON* const item);
​ ```
5. `cJSON_Duplicate`
​ `cJSON_Duplicate` creates a copy of a `cJSON` item. Use it on an existing item; `recurse=0` duplicates only the node, `recurse=1` duplicates the whole subtree. If `item` is `NULL`, it returns `NULL`.
